      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Constitutional law concerns the constitutional framework, the limits of government and individual rights. Statutory law consists of legislation. Administrative law concerns the powers, procedures and acts of public agencies. Case law develops through judicial decisions and their use as precedent.",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 3
            },
