    {
      "id": "constitution-and-jurisdiction",
      "title": "Rights, hierarchy and jurisdiction",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
          "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
          "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
          "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
          "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
          "page": 8
        }
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The deck calls the first ten constitutional amendments the Bill of Rights. It links constitutional interpretation to the relationship between government power and individual freedom. It also distinguishes federal, state and local law and uses animal regulation to illustrate that different levels may address different aspects of a subject.",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 3
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 5
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 6
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 8
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "key",
          "text": "Do not reduce jurisdiction to “federal always decides everything”. The animal example explicitly retains state authority over matters within state borders.",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 8
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Slide 7 gives an internally inconsistent sequence by treating Congress and the House of Representatives as separate successive institutions. It is not used here as a reliable bill-making flowchart. The supported distinction is that statutes are enacted legislation, unlike agency rules or judicial precedent.",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 6
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "summary": "Connect constitutional rights and limits on government with the distinct roles of federal, state and local law."
    },
    {
      "id": "fair-process",
      "title": "Fair laws and fair enforcement",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
          "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
          "page": 12
        },
        {
          "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
          "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
          "page": 13
        }
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The slides distinguish substantive due process, concerned with the fairness of laws themselves, from procedural due process, concerned with non-arbitrary enforcement through proper procedures. Their equity discussion focuses on fairness in resolving disputes.",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 12
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 13
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The adversarial system is described as opposing lawyers presenting their strongest arguments. Presumption of innocence and the prosecution’s burden of proof are taught in the context of an accused person. Do not apply that criminal-law description to every civil claim without further material.",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 12
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 13
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Examine the rule",
          "text": "What rights or restrictions does the rule create?",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 12
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 13
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Examine the procedure",
          "text": "How is the rule enforced and can the person respond?",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 12
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 13
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the parties’ roles",
          "text": "Who presents the accusation or claim and who contests it?",
          "source_refs": [
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 12
            },
            {
              "id": "996f2e3185d44f9a8474efb66c214055c8063b91b4b44233432877755a545bfb",
              "sha256": "35ea7ce930c9d65b360807b966ffa78c4a0c2d647ac5909ebe24015a0f61b88f",
              "page": 13
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "summary": "Distinguish fairness in the content of laws from fairness in enforcement, then relate both to dispute resolution."
    }
  ],
